<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bethlehem</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bethlehem is a Palestinian city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a>, about 10 kilometres south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. In the Bible it is the home of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a>'s family, and Christian tradition holds it to be the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a>, marked by the Church of the Nativity, first built under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine the Great</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> obtained it by treaty from the Ayyubid sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">al-Kamil</a> in 1229.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bethlehem.jpg" alt="Bethlehem" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Neil Ward · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Church_of_the_Nativity_(7703592746).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…called Asomtavruli, was in use by the fifth century, as shown by inscriptions at Bir el Qutt near <b>Bethlehem</b> and at the Bolnisi Sioni church, dated 493–494, and the Martyrdom of the Holy Queen Shushanik, written in the late fifth century, is the oldest surviving work of Georgian…</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-iberia">Kingdom of Iberia · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>When Godfrey died in July 1100, his brother Baldwin, count of Edessa, came south and was crowned King Baldwin I at <b>Bethlehem</b> on Christmas Day 1100.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Judah’s territory covered the southern highlands around Jerusalem, Hebron and <b>Bethlehem</b>, the low hills of the Shephelah to the west and the arid Negev to the south.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-judah">Kingdom of Judah · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The carol is sung by three women of <b>Bethlehem</b>, who come on stage with their children just after an angel has warned Joseph to take his family to Egypt; it is a lullaby of the mothers whose children are about to die in the Massacre of the Innocents,…</blockquote><a href="/songs/coventry-carol">Coventry Carol</a></li><li><blockquote>It draws on the prophecies of Isaiah, which in Christian interpretation foretell the Incarnation of Jesus, and on the Tree of Jesse, the traditional image of the descent of Jesus from Jesse of <b>Bethlehem</b>, father of King David, much loved in medieval religious art.</blockquote><a href="/songs/es-ist-ein-ros-entsprungen">Es ist ein Ros entsprungen</a></li><li><blockquote>A Christmas hymn that calls the faithful to come joyfully to <b>Bethlehem</b> and worship the newborn Christ.</blockquote><a href="/songs/o-come-all-ye-faithful">O Come, All Ye Faithful</a></li></ul></section>
